; Knife table — Counter-Strike 1.6 reference values (melee: no magazine).
; Scalars: https://csjs.live/weapons/knife (slash 15/20, stab 65, backstab x3,
; slash reach 48 u, stab reach 32 u, 250 u/s, no wall penetration).
; Code constants: https://github.com/s1lentq/ReGameDLL_CS
; - regamedll/dlls/weapons.h: KNIFE_STAB_DAMAGE 65, KNIFE_SWING_DAMAGE 15,
;   KNIFE_SWING_DAMAGE_FAST 20, KNIFE_STAB_DISTANCE 32, KNIFE_SWING_DISTANCE
;   48, KNIFE_BACKSTAB_MULTIPLIER 3 (dot > 0.8 behind target), KNIFE_MAX_SPEED
;   250.
; - regamedll/dlls/wpn_shared/wpn_knife.cpp: PrimaryAttack Swing (slash,
;   0.35-0.4 s cadence), SecondaryAttack Stab (1.0-1.1 s cadence);
;   m_iClip = WEAPON_NOCLIP (no magazine).
; - regamedll/dlls/player.cpp TakeDamage: ARMOR_RATIO 0.5 x 1.7
;   (WEAPON_KNIFE) = 0.85.
; Conventions: Damage = stab 65, SecondaryDamage = fast slash 20, Rpm = 0
; (manual cadence, not cyclic), MagSize = 0 with EMPTY RecoilTable (length ==
; mag holds), ReserveAmmo = -1 (no ammo), RangeModifier = 1.0 (no falloff;
; reach is gated by MeleeRangeU 48), MaxWallThicknessU = 0 (never penetrates).
; HeadshotMult = 1.0: no reference documents melee head behavior; engine
; TraceAttack hitgroups technically apply, but competitive sources never rely
; on it. COMMUNITY CONSENSUS — revisit if evidence found.
[gd_resource type="Resource" script_class="WeaponData" load_steps=2 format=3]

